{
  "lesson": {
    "id": "stub-pinn-convection",
    "title": "Train a PINN on the convection equation",
    "goal": "train a PINN on the convection equation",
    "workdir": "demo/pinn",
    "libraries": {
      "torch": "2.1"
    }
  },
  "sources": [
    {
      "id": "src-video",
      "kind": "video",
      "title": "Physics-informed neural networks: convection in PyTorch (stub)",
      "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=STUB_PINN_VID",
      "videoId": "STUB_PINN_VID"
    },
    {
      "id": "src-paper",
      "kind": "paper",
      "title": "Characterizing possible failure modes in physics-informed neural networks",
      "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.01050"
    }
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "index": 0,
      "title": "Create the training script",
      "instructions": "Create pinn_convection.py in your project folder.",
      "video": {
        "sourceId": "src-video",
        "start": 0,
        "end": 40
      },
      "checks": [
        {
          "id": "s1c1",
          "type": "screen_contains",
          "label": "pinn_convection.py open",
          "pattern": "pinn_convection\\.py",
          "app": "Code"
        }
      ],
      "targets": [],
      "hints": [
        "Make a new file named pinn_convection.py next to requirements.txt."
      ],
      "precision_checks": [
        {
          "id": "s1p1",
          "type": "file_exists",
          "label": "pinn_convection.py exists",
          "file": "pinn_convection.py"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "index": 1,
      "title": "Build the MLP",
      "instructions": "Define a fully connected network with tanh activations that maps (x, t) to u.",
      "video": {
        "sourceId": "src-video",
        "start": 40,
        "end": 120
      },
      "checks": [
        {
          "id": "s2c1",
          "type": "screen_contains",
          "label": "has Linear layers",
          "pattern": "nn\\.Linear",
          "app": "Code"
        },
        {
          "id": "s2c2",
          "type": "screen_contains",
          "label": "uses tanh",
          "pattern": "nn\\.Tanh|torch\\.tanh",
          "app": "Code"
        }
      ],
      "targets": [
        {
          "file": "pinn_convection.py",
          "match": "class \\w+\\(nn\\.Module\\)|nn\\.Sequential",
          "caption": "Two inputs (x, t), one output u",
          "app": "Code"
        }
      ],
      "explanations": [
        {
          "topic": "why tanh",
          "t": 95,
          "sourceId": "src-video"
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "What activation keeps second derivatives smooth?",
        "He builds the network at 1:05.",
        "Use nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(2, 50), nn.Tanh(), ..., nn.Linear(50, 1))."
      ],
      "precision_checks": [
        {
          "id": "s2p1",
          "type": "file_contains",
          "label": "has Linear layers",
          "file": "pinn_convection.py",
          "pattern": "nn\\.Linear"
        },
        {
          "id": "s2p2",
          "type": "file_contains",
          "label": "uses tanh",
          "file": "pinn_convection.py",
          "pattern": "nn\\.Tanh|torch\\.tanh"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "index": 2,
      "title": "Sample collocation points",
      "instructions": "Sample random (x, t) points in the domain and mark them requires_grad.",
      "video": {
        "sourceId": "src-video",
        "start": 120,
        "end": 200
      },
      "checks": [
        {
          "id": "s3c1",
          "type": "screen_contains",
          "label": "samples random points",
          "pattern": "torch\\.rand",
          "app": "Code"
        },
        {
          "id": "s3c2",
          "type": "screen_contains",
          "label": "points require grad",
          "pattern": "requires_grad",
          "app": "Code"
        }
      ],
      "targets": [
        {
          "file": "pinn_convection.py",
          "match": "torch\\.rand",
          "caption": "x in [0, 2π], t in [0, 1]",
          "app": "Code"
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "The residual needs derivatives with respect to the inputs.",
        "Call .requires_grad_(True) on the sampled tensors."
      ],
      "precision_checks": [
        {
          "id": "s3p1",
          "type": "file_contains",
          "label": "samples random points",
          "file": "pinn_convection.py",
          "pattern": "torch\\.rand"
        },
        {
          "id": "s3p2",
          "type": "file_contains",
          "label": "points require grad",
          "file": "pinn_convection.py",
          "pattern": "requires_grad"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "index": 3,
      "title": "Write the PDE residual",
      "instructions": "Use autograd for u_t and u_x, then return u_t + β·u_x.",
      "video": {
        "sourceId": "src-video",
        "start": 200,
        "end": 310
      },
      "checks": [
        {
          "id": "s4c1",
          "type": "screen_contains",
          "label": "computes u_t with autograd",
          "pattern": "autograd\\.grad",
          "app": "Code"
        },
        {
          "id": "s4c2",
          "type": "screen_contains",
          "label": "residual includes β·u_x",
          "pattern": "u_t\\s*\\+\\s*\\w*\\s*\\*\\s*u_x",
          "app": "Code"
        }
      ],
      "targets": [
        {
          "file": "pinn_convection.py",
          "match": "def pde_residual",
          "caption": "Write the residual · u_t + β·u_x",
          "app": "Code"
        }
      ],
      "explanations": [
        {
          "topic": "autograd for derivatives",
          "t": 240,
          "sourceId": "src-video"
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Which two derivatives appear in the convection equation?",
        "He writes the residual at 3:40.",
        "Section 2 of the paper states the PDE.",
        "return u_t + beta * u_x"
      ],
      "common_mistakes": [
        "u_t - beta * u_x (wrong sign)",
        "forgetting create_graph=True"
      ],
      "precision_checks": [
        {
          "id": "s4p1",
          "type": "file_contains",
          "label": "computes u_t with autograd",
          "file": "pinn_convection.py",
          "pattern": "autograd\\.grad"
        },
        {
          "id": "s4p2",
          "type": "file_contains",
          "label": "residual includes β·u_x",
          "file": "pinn_convection.py",
          "pattern": "u_t\\s*\\+\\s*\\w*\\s*\\*\\s*u_x"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "index": 4,
      "title": "Train at β = 1",
      "instructions": "Run the script with tut run and watch the loss fall.",
      "video": {
        "sourceId": "src-video",
        "start": 310,
        "end": 380
      },
      "checks": [
        {
          "id": "s5c1",
          "type": "metric_threshold",
          "label": "loss < 1e-2",
          "metric": "loss",
          "op": "<",
          "value": 0.01,
          "metric_pattern": "epoch\\s+(?P<step>\\d+).*?loss\\s+(?P<value>[0-9.eE+-]+)"
        }
      ],
      "targets": [
        {
          "file": "pinn_convection.py",
          "match": "def train|for epoch",
          "caption": "Run: tut run python pinn_convection.py --beta 1",
          "app": "Code"
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Run it through the wrapper: tut run python pinn_convection.py --beta 1"
      ],
      "precision_checks": [
        {
          "id": "s5p1",
          "type": "command_exit_ok",
          "label": "script runs",
          "command": "python pinn_convection.py --beta 1"
        },
        {
          "id": "s5p2",
          "type": "metric_threshold",
          "label": "loss < 1e-2",
          "metric": "loss",
          "op": "<",
          "value": 0.01
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "index": 5,
      "title": "Scale up to β = 30",
      "instructions": "Train at β = 30 until the loss drops below 1e-2.",
      "video": {
        "sourceId": "src-video",
        "start": 380,
        "end": 480
      },
      "checks": [
        {
          "id": "s6c1",
          "type": "metric_trend",
          "label": "loss still dropping",
          "metric": "loss",
          "trend": "not_flat",
          "window": 1500,
          "metric_pattern": "epoch\\s+(?P<step>\\d+).*?loss\\s+(?P<value>[0-9.eE+-]+)"
        },
        {
          "id": "s6c2",
          "type": "metric_threshold",
          "label": "loss < 1e-2",
          "metric": "loss",
          "op": "<",
          "value": 0.01,
          "by_step": 4000,
          "metric_pattern": "epoch\\s+(?P<step>\\d+).*?loss\\s+(?P<value>[0-9.eE+-]+)"
        }
      ],
      "targets": [
        {
          "file": "pinn_convection.py",
          "match": "def train|for epoch",
          "caption": "Add a β curriculum here",
          "app": "Code"
        }
      ],
      "explanations": [
        {
          "topic": "curriculum regularization",
          "t": 455,
          "sourceId": "src-video"
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Does the loss plateau? What makes β = 30 harder than β = 1?",
        "He explains the failure at 7:35.",
        "Krishnapriyan et al. (NeurIPS 2021) train with a β curriculum.",
        "for beta in [1, 5, 10, 20, 30]: train(model, beta, epochs)"
      ],
      "common_mistakes": [
        "training directly at β = 30",
        "lowering the learning rate instead of a curriculum"
      ]
    }
  ]
}